Why chunk overlap helps:

Prevents context loss: If a meaningful phrase or sentence spans the end of one chunk and the start of another, it could be lost without overlap.

Improves semantic integrity: Embeddings are better when the chunk includes enough coherent context.

Better retrieval recall: Overlap helps ensure that important phrases appear in at least one complete chunk, increasing chances of retrieval during search.

🔁 Recommended overlap size:

10–30% overlap is typical.

For a chunk size of 100 words, try 20–30 words overlap.




Is 100 a Good Chunk Size?

100 words is on the small side for chunking, and might not always be optimal.

🔍 Considerations:
Chunk Size (words)	Pros	Cons
<100	Fast retrieval, very focused chunks	May lose semantic meaning, too granular
100–300	Good balance between granularity and context	Common default range
>300	Better semantic coherence	Slower embedding/search; may dilute focus
📌 Recommendation:

Try chunk size of 200–300 words with 20–30 word overlap.

You can fine-tune it based on your PDF content style (e.g., legal docs vs. blog articles).